                <pb facs="0430" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/864: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-28T09:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 28,
                                1919, 9 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s August 20, 6 p.m. Commander Gayler left 25th for Washington via Cuba
                    and Key West with protocol, article 3, section 2 of which should read, after
                    “Haiti” as of December 31, 1916 as acknowledged by the Haitian Government on the
                    12th of April 1919”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
